# Trivy ignore file for vulnerabilities without available fixes
# These are OS-level vulnerabilities in Ubuntu 24.04 that don't have patches yet

# coreutils - low severity, very old CVE
CVE-2016-2781

# curl vulnerabilities - waiting for Ubuntu patches
CVE-2025-0167
CVE-2025-10148
CVE-2025-9086

# gpgv - low priority
CVE-2022-3219

# libgcrypt20 - waiting for Ubuntu patches
CVE-2024-2236

# libpam - waiting for Ubuntu patches
CVE-2025-8941

# openssl/libssl3t64 - waiting for Ubuntu patches
CVE-2024-41996

# login/passwd - waiting for Ubuntu patches
CVE-2024-56433

# tar - waiting for Ubuntu patches
CVE-2025-45582

# libexpat1 - waiting for Ubuntu patches
CVE-2025-66382

# sigstore/timestamp-authority - no fix available yet (v1.2.9 is latest)
CVE-2025-66564

# google.golang.org/grpc - CRITICAL, in vendored Traefik binary (not our code)
# gRPC-Go authorization bypass via missing leading slash in :path
# Traefik v3.6.11 does not yet bundle grpc >= v1.79.3
# https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-33186
CVE-2026-33186
# Trivy surfaces the same issue under Traefik's downstream advisory ID.
# Keep this entry alongside the CVE so both aliases are suppressed until
# Traefik ships a patched release.
# https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-46wh-3698-f2cx
GHSA-46wh-3698-f2cx

# github.com/docker/docker - HIGH, AuthZ plugin bypass with oversized request bodies
# AC image bundles Docker client libraries but does not expose AuthZ plugins
# https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-34040
CVE-2026-34040

# github.com/traefik/traefik/v3 - HIGH, in vendored Traefik binary
# Waiting for Traefik v3 patch release
# https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-32305
CVE-2026-32305

# github.com/go-jose/go-jose/v4 - HIGH, in vendored Traefik binary only.
# DoS panic on JWE decryption with certain key-wrap alg + empty encrypted_key.
# Our endpoints module is already on go-jose v4.1.4 (the fixed version), but
# the Traefik AMD64 binary downloaded in Dockerfile.ac.aws still ships v4.1.3.
# Traefik v3.6.12 still bundles go-jose v4.1.3.
# Wait for a Traefik release bundling go-jose >= v4.1.4 to remove this entry.
# https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-34986
CVE-2026-34986

# go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk - FALSE POSITIVE
# CVE-2026-39883 (PATH hijacking via kenv on BSD) is fixed in v1.43.0.
# We are on v1.43.0. Trivy's database incorrectly flags it — the affected
# range is < 1.43.0. Remove this entry once Trivy's DB is corrected.
# https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-39883
CVE-2026-39883
